# Knowledge Vault

Open [START-HERE.md](START-HERE.md) in Obsidian or point an agent at [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md).
This is a working vault, not the [core engineering checkout](https://github.com/bitpantry/knowledge-base).

## What belongs here

`catalog/` records sources and where to find them. `knowledge/` contains concepts, evidence,
decisions and interpretations. `extensions/` starts empty apart from its README;
add a domain extension only when you need one. Keep originals in their source systems.
If using Git, track approved records and extensions. Do not commit credentials,
raw source material, staging files, or anything the repository audience is not authorized to see.
A private repository does not authorize sharing client material.

## Update the core

From the vault folder, run these commands to **preview** a change:

```sh
python3 -B core/vault.py install account-management
python3 -B core/vault.py update account-management
python3 -B core/vault.py update
```

Add `--if-preview TOKEN_FROM_PREVIEW` to the same command to apply.
A general update includes the core and only package-managed extensions already
installed. Installing an extension adds its entry link to `START-HERE.md`.
It never classifies existing records; an agent proposes matches separately using
the [reconciliation workflow](core/RECONCILE.md).

The manager verifies the shipped files against the package receipts and stops
on local edits. It does not replace live records, settings, or custom docs.
The core receipt is `.core-release.json`; extension receipts live in their
extension folders. Track receipts if you track the vault in Git.

Run the checks below and review the diff before committing. Do not run the
updater concurrently with other edits or Git operations. If an update was
interrupted, compare with a known good checkout before retrying. These are beta packages, not a backward-compatibility guarantee. Read the
package notes before applying; any data conversion needs separate review and
testing.

```sh
python3 -B core/catalog.py check
python3 -B core/concepts.py check
python3 -B core/reconcile_extension.py check
```
